+/**
+ * Residual-work contract for mutual-TLS client authentication against the certificate registered for the
+ * client itself (RFC 8705, section 2.2), as opposed to the already shipped method that chains the presented
+ * certificate up to a certificate authority (RFC 8705, section 2.1).
+ * <p>
+ * Every {@code @Test} below is meant to be <em>independently</em> satisfiable, so that the number of passing
+ * tests measures how much of the work is still missing rather than acting as one boolean wearing nine names.
+ * In particular the behaviour axes (B1..B4) never read the shipped profile JSON and never require the
+ * ServiceLoader registration; the registration axis (A2) never requires the class-scan axis (A1); and the
+ * JSON axes (A4, A5) never require any of the others.
+ * <p>
+ * The implementation under test is never referenced by class name. It is discovered by the union of two
+ * name-independent routes:
+ * <ol>
+ *     <li>a scan of the compiled classes directory of this module for concrete {@link ClientAuthenticator}
+ *     implementations that are absent from the baseline measured on the pristine tree at the base commit;</li>
+ *     <li>the provider SPI: {@link ClientAuthenticatorFactory} ids resolvable through the session factory
+ *     that are absent from the baseline measured on the pristine tree at the base commit.</li>
+ * </ol>
+ * When neither route finds anything the behaviour axes fail with an explicit message; they never error.
+ * <p>
+ * Every behaviour axis exercises the authenticator in the state the runtime puts it in: the token endpoint
+ * runs client authentication as an authentication flow, so the provider is obtained from its factory with
+ * {@code create(session)}, the certificate chain is offered both through the
+ * {@link X509ClientCertificateLookup} SPI and through {@link HttpRequest#getClientCertificateChain()}, the
+ * request carries a form-encoded {@code client_id}, and the realm resolves that id to an enabled client that
+ * has a certificate registered under the shipped PEM attribute. That set-up lives in one place,
+ * {@link #authenticate(X509Certificate[], String)}, so no axis added later can forget it.
+ */
